  "count_definition": "Actual final executions across O0/O2 and P/E cores, not unique inputs. Every pair compares represented GPR/flag, segment/system, active event and RAM state against independent original bytes. Compiler returns and VERR/VERW success/rejection counts are subsets of those pairs.",
  "native_boundary": "266 functions per optimization profile: 17 APIs, both address sizes, all seven segment prefixes, independent table operand sizes and live/dead verification results. Per-function cases combine CPL0/CPL3, clear/AC/UMIP state, eight operand/descriptor memory configurations and 16 selector or four scalar/table input images.",
  "state_effects": "Observe CR0 low-bit changes, GDTR/IDTR values including legacy operand truncation, LDTR/TR cache changes, LTR descriptor busy-bit writes, native ZF and exact memory stores. Source/cached segment controls, privilege/UMIP, read-only/cross-page/missing operands and descriptor faults retain native ordering.",
  "negative_controls": "Every profile rejects zeroed address transport before an intact instruction and an inverted returned VERR ZF. Every positive case independently checks its declared effective offset at the instruction boundary, then compares the original instruction state.",
  "fault_observation": "Original #NP/#GP/#PF/#AC handlers execute completed OUT. Both saved restart PCs are authenticated before normalizing only that frame PC; inactive exception payload is excluded only after proving neither pending nor injected. Other represented event fields and complete RAM remain compared.",
  "cs_address_contract": "CS.base places code at linear 0x10000 while relative code16 RIPs fit 64 KiB. Linear debug addresses are distinct from guest RIP. Flat fault handlers and the existing shared helpers are unchanged.",
